WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.625 --> 00:00:09.325
Here’s how working with us works.

2
00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:22.405
Take Hakim.

3
00:00:22.445 --> 00:00:24.005
He runs a renovation company.

4
00:00:24.345 --> 00:00:25.325
Last time,

5
00:00:25.365 --> 00:00:26.545
an agency quoted him

6
00:00:26.585 --> 00:00:28.045
about eight thousand,

7
00:00:28.085 --> 00:00:29.185
about six weeks.

8
00:00:29.545 --> 00:00:31.025
It took fifteen thousand

9
00:00:31.065 --> 00:00:32.685
and four months.

10
00:00:33.085 --> 00:00:33.505
So now

11
00:00:33.545 --> 00:00:35.305
he wants the cheapest quote.

12
00:00:35.665 --> 00:00:36.565
Less to lose, right?

13
00:00:36.605 --> 00:00:37.585
No.

14
00:00:38.265 --> 00:00:39.985
Cheap isn’t what burned him.

15
00:00:40.025 --> 00:00:40.485
Watch.

16
00:00:41.037 --> 00:00:42.717
It starts with one message,

17
00:00:43.097 --> 00:00:44.477
on WhatsApp or email.

18
00:00:44.957 --> 00:00:46.537
Just describe the problem.

19
00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:48.490
Hakim types one line:

20
00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.690
my website gets no calls.

21
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.610
We reply the same day,

22
00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:53.850
and one senior lead

23
00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.310
stays with him to delivery.

24
00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:56.430
But the last agency

25
00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.130
was friendly on day one too.

26
00:00:58.570 --> 00:00:59.270
So what does he get

27
00:00:59.310 --> 00:00:59.870
in writing?

28
00:01:00.247 --> 00:01:01.687
Before he pays a thing,

29
00:01:01.987 --> 00:01:03.467
his lead puts it in writing.

30
00:01:10.287 --> 00:01:10.887
The date:

31
00:01:11.327 --> 00:01:12.647
live in two weeks.

32
00:01:13.107 --> 00:01:13.887
No estimate.

33
00:01:14.327 --> 00:01:15.527
Hakim reads it twice,

34
00:01:15.727 --> 00:01:16.827
hunting for the catch.

35
00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:17.827
Even hosting

36
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:19.287
is flagged up front,

37
00:01:19.327 --> 00:01:20.007
at cost.

38
00:01:20.487 --> 00:01:21.267
He says yes.

39
00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:22.567
So he pays,

40
00:01:22.807 --> 00:01:23.607
and work starts

41
00:01:23.647 --> 00:01:25.087
within 24 hours.

42
00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:36.840
His job:

43
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.700
feedback at each checkpoint.

44
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:39.670
Ours:

45
00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:40.700
the date.

46
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.040
Two weeks later,

47
00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.120
the site is live.

48
00:01:43.448 --> 00:01:45.248
But what if we’d missed that date,

49
00:01:45.488 --> 00:01:47.008
or the scope we agreed?

50
00:01:47.279 --> 00:01:48.659
He’d get his money back.

51
00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:50.739
That’s the guarantee,

52
00:01:51.199 --> 00:01:51.919
in writing.

53
00:01:57.199 --> 00:01:58.179
Why offer it?

54
00:02:04.279 --> 00:02:05.499
But once it’s live,

55
00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:06.579
who owns it?

56
00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:07.325
He does.

57
00:02:07.765 --> 00:02:08.885
On the final payment,

58
00:02:09.285 --> 00:02:10.385
everything we made

59
00:02:10.425 --> 00:02:11.245
is his.

60
00:02:15.222 --> 00:02:16.382
No licence.

61
00:02:16.422 --> 00:02:17.362
No subscription.

62
00:02:17.922 --> 00:02:18.862
And if you start smaller,

63
00:02:18.902 --> 00:02:20.022
with an audit,

64
00:02:20.342 --> 00:02:21.222
that fee comes off

65
00:02:21.262 --> 00:02:22.362
the build that follows,

66
00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.722
if you go ahead within

67
00:02:23.762 --> 00:02:24.722
the offer period.

68
00:02:28.392 --> 00:02:30.072
So what burned him last time?

69
00:02:30.432 --> 00:02:31.372
Not the cheap quote.

70
00:02:31.612 --> 00:02:32.872
It was one word:

71
00:02:33.392 --> 00:02:33.692
about.

72
00:02:34.112 --> 00:02:35.132
About a price,

73
00:02:35.432 --> 00:02:36.472
about a date,

74
00:02:36.512 --> 00:02:38.052
so both could grow.

75
00:02:38.452 --> 00:02:39.232
Take out the about,

76
00:02:39.272 --> 00:02:40.292
and put money

77
00:02:40.332 --> 00:02:41.332
behind the date.

78
00:02:41.592 --> 00:02:42.552
That’s how you hire

79
00:02:42.592 --> 00:02:43.812
without getting burned.

80
00:02:44.209 --> 00:02:46.189
Now, what would you fix first?

